  "weights_rationale": "House default 15/50/35, restored deliberately from the 25/50/25 used on 9-Aug-2026 and matching the model of record. The 9-Aug run raised bear weight to 25% ahead of an uncertain H1 print; that print (13-Aug) landed clearly ahead -- 21% CC net revenue growth, 24% volume growth, guidance RAISED to 21-23% CC, Digital reaccelerating from its record-low Q1 -- which resolved the specific uncertainty the extra bear weight was insuring against. Bear stays at 15% and not lower because the take-rate question is genuinely unresolved (management's 'volume tiering' framing cannot yet be independently verified against competitive discounting) and because the balance sheet carries no solvency or refinancing risk at all -- the bear case is margin and growth compression, never distress. Bull at 35% because the bull path needs only the already-observed Platforms/Unified Commerce trajectory to persist, not several independent things to go right.",
